{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.golden_of_sqrt5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.golden_of_sqrt5","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L179-L185","doc":"The golden element `(1+s)/2` satisfies the fold relation `φ² = φ + 1`, tying\nthe two sections: the fold parameter of `qi` at the first flat connection is the\ngolden ratio of the same `√5` that carries the normalization identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.vacuum_modulus_identity_second","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.vacuum_modulus_identity_second","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L172-L177","doc":"The vacuum-node modulus identity, second flat connection (Galois conjugate):\n`(4/5)·((10+2s)/16)·(10−2s) = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.vacuum_modulus_identity_first","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.vacuum_modulus_identity_first","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L165-L170","doc":"The vacuum-node modulus identity, first flat connection, written out:\n`(4/5)·((10−2s)/16)·(10+2s) = 4` — `|A₁(1)|² · D_Ê₈(ζ)² = 4·[1]²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.core_normalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.core_normalization","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L155-L163","doc":"**Core normalization identity**: for `s² = 5` (a square root of 5 in any\ncharacteristic-zero field), `(10 − 2s)(10 + 2s) = 80`.  Under `s = √5` this is\nexactly `((2/√5)·sin(π/5))² · D_Ê₈(ζ)² = 4` — i.e. the vacuum-node case of the\nfactor-2-corrected modulus identity `|A_m(mark)|·D_Ê₈(ζ^m) = 2·|[mark]_{ζ^m}|` —\nsince `sin²(π/5) = (10−2√5)/16` and `D_Ê₈(ζ)² = 10+2√5` (and Galois-symmetrically\nfor the second flat connection, `sin²(2π/5) = (10+2√5)/16`, `D² = 10−2√5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.D2_E8_second_fold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.D2_E8_second_fold","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L140-L147","doc":"`D_Ê₈²` at the second fold is `12 − 4φ` (= `10 − 2√5`): the Galois conjugate\nof `8 + 4φ` under `φ ↦ 1 − φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi'_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi'_six","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L137-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi'_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi'_five","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L134-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi'_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi'_four","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L131-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi'_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi'_three","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L128-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.fold_multiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.fold_multiplicity","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L117-L124","doc":"**Fold multiplicity**: `D_Ê₈² = 2·D_MTC²` — the affine-Ê₈ node set folds 2:1\nonto the r = 5 alcove (node 5 → 0).  This is the exact origin of the global\nfactor 2 (resp. √2) correcting the conjectured modulus identification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.D2_MTC_first_fold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.D2_MTC_first_fold","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L110-L115","doc":"`D_MTC²`: the sum of `[α]²` over the r = 5 alcove `{1,2,3,4}` is `4 + 2φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.D2_E8_first_fold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.D2_E8_first_fold","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L102-L108","doc":"`D_Ê₈²` at the first fold: the sum of `[mark]²` over the 9 nodes is `8 + 4φ`\n(= `10 + 2√5` at `φ = (1+√5)/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi_six","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L99-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi_five","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L96-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi_four","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L93-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_phi_three","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L90-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.sum_marks_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.sum_marks_sq","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L85-L86","doc":"`Σ mark² = 120 = |2I|` — the `q = 1` group-side anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.marks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.marks","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L82-L83","doc":"The affine-Ê₈ marks (= dimensions of the 2I irreps), trivial node included. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_six","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L77-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_five","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L74-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_four","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L71-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_three","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_two","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi_zero","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold.qi","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneLRModulusFold.lean#L60-L65","doc":"Chebyshev-recursed quantum integer `[n]` at a fold parameter `t = ζ + ζ⁻¹`:\n`[0] = 0`, `[1] = 1`, `[n+2] = t·[n+1] − [n]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}